  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/22-spiny-eels/macrognathus_taeniagaster_en/",
      "html": "<p>Macrognathus taeniagaster is a small spiny eel from Thailand. It can change colour very fast: the same fish can be uniformly beige in one moment and in the next show an almost white back and a dark belly.</p><p>Lexicon: Macrognathus is ancient Greek and means \"with big jaw\"; taeniagaster is ancient Greek and means \"with banded belly\"; circumcinctus is Latin and means \"girdled thorough\".</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "beforeYouBuy",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/22-spiny-eels/macrognathus_taeniagaster_en/",
      "html": "<p>Basically speaking, the spiny eels of Asia can be divided in two groups: the small species belonging to the genus Macrognathus that usually reach only 10-15 cm total length and the large species of the genus Mastacembelus that grow to more than 40 cm (maximum length reported: 100 cm).</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/22-spiny-eels/macrognathus_taeniagaster_en/",
      "html": "<p>Thailand.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "maintenance",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/22-spiny-eels/macrognathus_taeniagaster_en/",
      "html": "<p>Keeping these spiny eels is very easy. The fish like the company of their own kind and often share the same hiding place.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/22-spiny-eels/macrognathus_taeniagaster_en/",
      "html": "<p>Macrognathus feed readily on any type of frozen and live fish food. Very small fish are taken as food.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/22-spiny-eels/macrognathus_taeniagaster_en/",
      "html": "<p>In general the spiny eels are very peaceful towards tankmates and are very suitable for community tanks.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "dimorphism",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/22-spiny-eels/macrognathus_taeniagaster_en/",
      "html": "<p>Males stay smaller than the females and are much more slim.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/22-spiny-eels/macrognathus_taeniagaster_en/",
      "html": "<p>The fish spawn near the water surface in the roots of floating fern and similar plants. It is possible to breed these fish in aquaria, but this is rarely done.</p>"
    }
  ],
